<title>USA: Nucor raises steel prices.</title>
<headline>Nucor raises steel prices.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nucor Corp raised steel prices by $10 per ton when it opened its first-quarter order book over the weekend, President John Correnti told Reuters Monday.</p>
<p>Correnti said the price increase affects hot-rolled, cold-rolled and galvanized steel products. It takes effect immediately on new orders, but orders that were on the books for at least 60 days will not be subject to the increase.</p>
<p>Correnti said Nucor raised prices because demand continues to be strong.</p>
<p>-- Pittsburgh newsroom 412-471-7088</p>
</text>
